course: dictionary
lesson: 12729
title: Dreaded: feared, or just disliked
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dreaded comes from the verb dread, which means to feel great fear about something that is coming. When dreaded is placed before a noun, it describes something people fear or do not want to face. «The dreaded storm arrived at midnight.» The word tells you the storm was feared, so people were worried about it.
explain: Context shows you the mood. «The dreaded dragon roared from its cave» sounds truly frightening, so dreaded means feared very much. But read «the dreaded Monday morning». Nobody is really scared of Monday. The writer is joking about something annoying, so dreaded means disliked in a playful, mock-scary way.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simple word. Put «feared» or «much disliked» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Then you know whether the writer means real fear or a joke.
fact: Dreaded means feared very much, or something people do not want to happen or face.
fact: «The dreaded day» means a day people fear.
fact: In informal, joking talk, «the dreaded homework» means homework that is annoying, not truly scary.
fact: Dreaded is also the past form of the verb dread.
fact: Much-dreaded is used in the same way: «the much-dreaded test» means a test people fear very much.
exercise: «The dreaded wolf howled at the edge of the forest.» What does dreaded mean here? | Very friendly | Sleepy | *Feared very much | Lost and hungry
exercise: Mia says, «It's the dreaded homework again!» What is the joke in her words? | It is a happy party | It is a secret for the teacher | *It is annoying, said in a mock-scary way | It is a dangerous monster
exercise: «Everyone hoped the dreaded storm would pass quickly.» Find and copy one word that means feared. | quickly | *dreaded | hoped | everyone
test: «The dreaded dentist's drill buzzed in the little room.» What does dreaded suggest? | *Something people fear | Something very quiet | A kind of sweet treat | Something people love
test: Which phrase uses dreaded in a joking way? | the dreaded night of the storm | *the dreaded vegetables at dinner | the dreaded avalanche on the mountain | the dreaded wolf in the woods
exam: In «the dreaded Monday morning», which swap for dreaded makes the best sense? | a morning with no school at all | a morning in the middle of June | *a morning people dislike | a morning people dream of
